MID_SE_Dit_Esm_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_C_001: Mm! These buns...so delicious, and so worth the\nwait to get them fresh from the oven!
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_C_002: Fabio did his best to ruin the taste with his\nbitterness...but they're too delicious for that!
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_C_003: I'm the one who bought them, so why does he think\nhe gets a say anyway? It's my money and my mouth!
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_C_004: I just hope Sweetie doesn't catch me gobbling up\nthese buns like a little kid!
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_C_005: I detect sweetness in the air...
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_C_006: {SetColor=Gray}No! Not now! I better cram this last one before he\nsees! Mmph...{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_C_007: Hey, Sweetie! Looking for me? Just me—with\nnothing to hide!
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_C_008: Suspicious. No, no matter. What is this scent?
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_C_009: Scent? No scent here. Smells like...a heap of nothing!
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_C_010: Indeed? My nose led me this way. *sniff* Yes, the\nscent is coming from you.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_C_011: {SetColor=Gray}Is...is he sniffing me? It's...nice he's close...but... Oh,\nthis is too weird!{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_C_012: I ate them! I gobbled them up! I couldn't help it!
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_C_013: I did not call your actions into question. Tell me,\nthough. Are all the treats gone?
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_C_014: Uh... Yes? I crammed in the last one when you came\nup behind me!
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_C_015: So they are gone. I see.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_C_016: Sweetie... Do you—did you—want a treat?
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_C_017: I have a weakness for sweet, delicious foods. They\nare all I want to eat...
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_C_018: Really? Me too! Can't get enough!
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_C_019: Hmm... Here we go! Try this. It's called a date. It's\nno sweet bun, but it's still tasty!
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_C_020: Oh? Dried fruit... It is somewhat delicious.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_C_021: Hyehehe! It is, isn't it? I love these! Mmm...
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_C_022: You know what? We should get treats together. And\nnot tell Fabio!
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_001: So these are fried, not baked. The sweetness is\nmoderate...but I do like them.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_002: They're called "madazins." Never had 'em before, but\nthey are good!
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_003: Oh? You have not had them either? I had thought\nthey were of Dagda.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_004: Yes, but... I come from a small village far away from\nhere, remember? We don't eat anything like this.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_005: I see! I now understand why you so ravenously\ndevoured those buns. They were novel to you.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_006: Uh... No? I was just trying—no, never mind. Wait,\nSweetie? Something wrong?
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_007: I was just thinking of my sister. We often spend time\nthis way.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_008: Elfrida is skilled at baking. She...has the deft hand\nI lack.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_009: Ooh, baking? I want to try! And when I do, do you\nwant to be my taste tester?
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_010: If you wish it. Thanks to my sister, I am used to\nthat role.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_011: Well, there you go! That has me wondering, though...\nIs Elfrida much like me?
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_012: I was thinking just now that maybe that's why you\nrescued me. From getting eaten.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_013: She is quite unlike you.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_014: Sure... I guess it makes sense. She's your sister, so...\nShe's probably just as gorgeous.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_015: What a weird thing to ask. I know you saved me on\na whim.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_016: That is not accurate. It is because of something\nElfrida said, in fact.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_017: She would say that I am always causing\nothers trouble...
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_018: Well, she isn't really wrong. You are amazing, but...\na little bit of a handful. Uh, but keep going!
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_019: "Listen to the troubles of those in need," she said.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_020: I may be unable to change myself, but I can achieve\nat least that much, or so she told me.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_021: Since then, I have done my best to listen to the needs\nof others.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_022: So what you're saying is, thanks to your sister, you\nsaved me. I have to thank her somehow!
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_023: But...wait a second. When we were at that village\nwith the wild-dog problem, you...didn't do anything.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_024: I listened. That was surely enough.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_025: Uh, Sweetie? I think Elfrida was hoping you'd\nHELP PEOPLE, not just listen to them.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_026: Do you think so? Hmm... I have erred, then. If I do\nnot right my ways, it will invite her ire once more.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_027: Just try to keep it in mind, and you'll be fine! Though\nI'm not sure you're really a do-gooder, you know?
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_028: OK, here's what we'll do! We'll split the work!
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_029: If you can't take care of something, I will! Like when\nI mixed up those rotting fish guts into dog repellent.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_030: Is that proper? Elfrida's words were directed solely\nat me.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_031: Of course! I want to repay my debt to her, after all!
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_B_032: Ahh...
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_001: Ugh! It sounded so simple...why are they turning\nout like this?
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_002: Agh! Why do they burn so quickly? What am I\ndoing wrong?
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_003: Making treats, are you? They look familiar.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_004: I thought since you liked those madazins so much,\nI'd try making you some.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_005: I got the recipe from the baker. They're supposed to\ncook up just fine over a campfire...
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_006: I'm used to cooking fish over the fire, but this...\nisn't fish!
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_007: They appear excessively charred. They will likely\nbe bitter. I dislike bitter food.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_008: Wait! I'll try again. At least one of them will turn\nout OK!
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_009: A prime chance to test my mettle. I impale the dough\nand then roast it over the flame, yes?
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_010: What? You want to try? You know you don't\nhave to...
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_011: I simply wish to test my baking skills.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_012: Well, sure! I'd love to cook together. OK, it's on!
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_013: This is much trickier than I had anticipated. The\ndough is weak. It burns.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_014: I thought your idea to stoke the flames and really\nroast them would do the trick.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_015: Thing is, with fish, you can hear 'em sizzle, and you\nknow when they're done. These you have to watch.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_016: We're already out of dough, and none of them turned\nout well... I guess I'll just eat all these...whatevers.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_017: Ugh! Wow, that's bitter. They weren't even all that\nsweet to start with...
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_018: I will also sample them. Mm... *choke* *gag*\nHaaah... Haaah...
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_019: Sweetie! I'll eat them! You don't have to! I mean...\nthey're so bitter. You hate that!
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_020: You dislike them as well. I can see it in your eyes.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_021: Well, I can see it on your whole face! Besides, it's my\nmess, and I need to clean it up! By eating it!
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_022: We will divide and conquer. I will consume half.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_023: You said before you would shoulder half my burdens.\nTherefore it is only fair that I shoulder half of yours...
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_024: Sweetie, I'm so happy to hear you say that. Oh...\nthank you!
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_025: Sweetie? Are you alright? You don't look so hot.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_026: I have never experienced this level of distress.\nHowever, I yet live.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_027: That's...good. But I don't think we can get through all\nof these.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_028: I have an idea. Once you're done visiting Dagda, let's\nget your sister to teach us all about baking.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_029: I had never considered this. As always, the ideas you\nsuggest exceed the bounds of my imagination.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_030: But why not? I shall introduce you to Elfrida.
MID_SE_Dit_Esm_A_031: Really? It's a date! Let's bake!